 -k         keep intermediate temporary file(s)         -x         show licence details         -t[=][<n>] expand tab characters (tab-size <n> default is 4)      If no -c, -l, -C, -L or -N specified, -t is set automatically      If both -C & -L (or -c & -l) given, CR/LF is implied      If neither -c or -l given, auto-detection of input format {i.e. first                                      EOL sequence detected is used}.      If none of -C, -L, -N given, output is based on input format: see -H  autoreply   (CMDS/ELM)      no help of its own -- `autoreply on' and `autoreply off' are its whole vocabulary, plus a file of reply text; there is no help flag  back   (CMDS/GAMES)      no help of its own -- it takes no options; H at its prompt is the help  backgammon   (CMDS/GAMES)      $ backgammon -?      Syntax: backgammon [<opts>] [<file>]      Function: what do you think ?      Options:           -n        don't ask for instructions           -r        you play red           -w        you play white           -b        you play both sides           -p[rwb]   print board before red/white/both           -s <file> recover earlier game from <file>      If no -s is present, but <file> is specified, then      recover from <file>  bandit   (CMDS/GAMES)      no help of its own -- it has no help flag; `y' at its first question prints the instructions, and `q' at the bet prompt quits  banner   (CMDS)      no help of its own -- it takes the text to print and nothing else  banner1   (CMDS)      $ banner1 -?      Syntax: banner [<opts>] {<string>} [<opts>]      Function: prints a banner to stdout      Options:           -i          prints italic           -d          double size           -c=<char>   character           -s          use same character           -z          read strings from standard input           -z=<file>   read strings from <file>  basename   (CMDS)      $ basename -?      basename v1.0 (c) M.C.Gregorie, 1994   